8. Risks & Mitigation

· Performance on large plans: The lazy TEG approach avoids building the full O(M²) graph up front. Dijkstra explores only a small fraction. If needed, we can prune time instants that cannot lead to better paths (e.g., using earliest arrival at each node).
· Floating point precision: All time and capacity calculations use integer microseconds or decimal.Decimal to guarantee exact volume integrals, avoiding rounding errors.
· Discrepancies with real CGR: The MVP solves the exact optimal problem; it may find routes that real‑time heuristics miss. This is a feature, not a bug. The documentation will clarify the difference.

