3. Alignment with the MVP

· Physical models: physics.py implements the contact volume and transfer time calculations (Eqs. 1, 2, 3 from the theoretical document).
· Discretisation: discretize.py extracts all event instants from the contact plan and the bundle creation time.
· Lazy time‑expanded graph: teg.py never builds the full graph ahead of time. It generates (node, time) states on the fly during Dijkstra (waiting edges + transmission edges). This mirrors the TEG described in Appendix B, with the exact formula (B.2) simplified thanks to constant capacity.
· Correctness: The algorithm guarantees the earliest possible delivery (Theorem 1) because it explores every feasible state without omitting any solution.
· Extensibility: The modular design makes it straightforward to add multi‑bundle sequential routing with residual capacity updates (Appendix G) in a future iteration.

